{"name":"Crisp Wonton","hex":"#f3dcc6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"crisp","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Senses relating to curliness.\n Of hair: curling, especially in tight, stiff curls or ringlets; also , of a person: having hair curled in this manner.","Of hair: curling, especially in tight, stiff curls or ringlets; also , of a person: having hair curled in this manner."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Senses relating to something brittle.\n In full potato crisp: a thin slice of potato which has been deep-fried until it is brittle and crispy, and eaten when cool; they are typically packaged and sold as a snack.","In full potato crisp: a thin slice of potato which has been deep-fried until it is brittle and crispy, and eaten when cool; they are typically packaged and sold as a snack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crisp"},{"term":"wonton","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A Chinese dumpling, often stuffed with varieties of meat or seafood and vegetables."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wonton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Wonton","blocks":[{"text":"A wonton is a type of Chinese dumpling commonly found across regional styles of Chinese cuisine. It is also spelled wantan or wuntun, a transliteration from Cantonese wan4 tan1, and wenden from Shanghainese hhun den. Even though there are many different styles of wonton served throughout China, Cantonese wontons are the most popular in the West due to the predominance of Cantonese restaurants overseas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Pork_Steamed_Wontons.jpg/330px-Pork_Steamed_Wontons.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wonton","wikidata":"Q553905"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Wonton_1.JPG/500px-Wonton_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content